{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With the direct 0->3 edge missing, edge 5 carries the output path, so adding a 3x3 conv there gains much more (exp 1: +24) than when other paths exist."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0 is none, edge 3 is a main route to the output, so removing it is catastrophic (exp 3: -78) compared with redundant cells (exp 13: -1)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with a conv restores a direct input-to-output path, a bigger gain than replacing an existing parametric op (exp 8: +14 to +17)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading a parameter-free pool to a 3x3 conv helps a lot (exp 4: +6 to +12), whereas replacing a conv1x1 changes little (exp 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the edge was none opens a feature path (exp 6: +1 to +5), unlike replacing conv1x1 (exp 20: about 0)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading a 3x3 conv on the output edge to skip loses capacity (exp 11: -2 to -9), while replacing a conv1x1 is about neutral (exp 9)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op with a conv adds learnable capacity (exp 16: +5 to +11), which should beat the effect of replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the input conv 3x3 with skip removes early feature extraction and hurts on all datasets (exp 7: -5 to -8)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Reconnecting a removed edge with skip adds a useful path (exp 12: +5 to +10), more than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a direct input-to-output route via skip helps most when the edge was none (exp 15: +1 to +9)."}], "tok": 8036, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x3"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "skip_connect", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["none", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_con